# This directory contains content-addressed evidence, including production
# registries whose loaders require canonical JSON terminated by exactly one
# LF. Any end-of-line translation changes those bytes, so on a Windows host
# with core.autocrlf=true a zero-access declaration or production registry can
# become unreadable before the authority check it exists to perform is reached.
#
# -text disables conversion in both directions. Schema-v2 versions of the
# canonical production artifacts provide the one-time tracked blob change that
# also refreshes pre-existing worktrees when this rule is first introduced.
*.json -text
